# Git Keep File for Reports Directory

This file ensures that the reports directory structure is maintained in Git.

## Directory Structure:
- quality/     - Quality and performance reports
- cleanup/     - Cleanup and maintenance reports  
- transformation/ - System transformation reports
- compliance/  - Compliance and standards reports
- archive/     - Archived reports (older than 6 months)

## Guidelines:
- Keep this file to maintain directory structure
- All reports should follow the naming conventions in README.md
- Regular archival of old reports is recommended